Licence:    MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option. The texts are in LICENSE-MIT and
            LICENSE-APACHE in this folder, copied from the upstream commit.

Vendored on 2026-10-01 for Kairos task COLLIERY-T-1848 (initiative
COLLIERY-I-0264, the code index).

Files taken from upstream src/:

  symbols.rs    symbol kinds and the Symbol type
  parser.rs     the tree-sitter parser and the symbol queries
  callgraph.rs  the call graph (for COLLIERY-T-1849)

Nothing else is taken: not the MCP server, the LSP, the network, the neural
or embedding code, the persistence, the security rules or the frontend.

Changes from upstream:

  1. parser.rs: the language list is cut to Rust, Python, TypeScript, TSX and
     Go. The unit tests for the removed languages (and the JavaScript UTF-8
     signature test) are removed. The queries of the kept languages are not
     changed.
  2. symbols.rs and parser.rs: each Symbol also carries start_byte and
     end_byte, the byte range of its definition node. Each changed line is
     marked "KAIROS PATCH".
  3. parser.rs: the Rust query also captures `function_signature_item`, a
     trait method with no body, as a function. A call on a generic value
     resolves to that declaration (COLLIERY-T-1849). Marked "KAIROS PATCH".
  4. lib.rs and Cargo.toml are new. Cargo.toml lists only the dependencies of
     the three files.
  5. callgraph.rs: the tokenizer of extract_calls_from_macro_text is the free
     function macro_text_calls, with no change to what it finds. kairos-index
     uses it for the calls in the text of a Rust macro invocation
     (COLLIERY-T-1851). Marked "KAIROS PATCH".
